# Documentation hub

Canonical entry: `docs/README.md`.

## Do

- Update living docs linked from the hub (`getting-started`, `database`, `architecture`, `quality`, ops/product/domain pages)
- Put dated decisions in `context/` when they are not runbooks
- Move superseded plans to `docs/archive/` and point the hub/archive README at replacements

## Do not

- Add `COMPLETION_SUMMARY`, `REFACTORING_SUMMARY`, `CHART_FIX`, or similar one-off notes under `docs/`
- Invent a parallel process doc that contradicts `docs/database.md` or `.cursor/rules/prisma-migrations-only.mdc`
- Document `db push` as the default schema apply step (Prisma Migrate only)

When unsure where something belongs, add a short link from `docs/README.md` rather than a new top-level plan file.
